      "description": "Only one dynamic-looking preg_* exists (helpers.php:238) and its pattern is a static literal (/\\B(?=(\\d{2})+(?!\\d))/) with no user input in the pattern. The other SAST hits are string-argument false positives. No user input reaches a dynamic regex.",
      "remediation": {
        "summary": "No action."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "SCR-D09",
      "title": "DISMISSED: JavaScript XSS execution inside mPDF-rendered PDFs",
      "severity": "Info",
      "status": "dismissed",
      "discovered_by": "injection+verifier",
      "category": "Dismissed",
      "locations": [
        {
          "path": "app/Traits/MpdfTrait.php",
          "line": 1
        }
      ],
      "description": "mPDF does not execute <script>, so classic JS-XSS does not apply in the PDF context. The unescaped-input risk is reclassified as HTML/content injection (SCR-014) plus SSRF (SCR-006).",
      "remediation": {
        "summary": "No JS-XSS action; escaping fix tracked under SCR-006 and SCR-014."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "SCR-D10",
      "title": "DISMISSED: FdoneformController::ministryLetterAnswerStore upload",
      "severity": "Info",
      "status": "dismissed",
      "discovered_by": "injection",
      "category": "Dismissed",
      "locations": [
        {
          "path": "app/Http/Controllers/NGO/FdoneformController.php",
          "line": 1
        }
      ],
      "description": "Regenerates the filename with a safe extension allow-list, so the getClientOriginalName() RCE pattern of SCR-001/SCR-004 does not apply here.",
      "remediation": {
        "summary": "No action; this is the correct pattern the other upload sites should adopt."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "SCR-D11",
      "title": "DISMISSED: singleStaffDetailsInformationEexecutiveUpdate upload sink",
      "severity": "Info",
      "status": "dismissed",
      "discovered_by": "injection",
      "category": "Dismissed",
      "locations": [
        {
          "path": "app/Http/Controllers/NGO/FdoneformController.php",
          "line": 1448
        }
      ],
      "description": "Unreachable - the route mapping to this method is commented out, so the upload sink cannot be triggered.",
      "remediation": {
        "summary": "No action; remove the dead code to reduce confusion."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "SCR-D12",
      "title": "DISMISSED (as standalone): 6-digit email-verification token",
      "severity": "Info",
      "status": "dismissed",
      "discovered_by": "authz+verifier",
      "category": "Dismissed",
      "locations": [
        {
          "path": "app/Http/Controllers/Api/AuthController.php",
          "line": 93
        }
      ],
      "description": "random_int(100000,999999) is a CSPRNG so values are unpredictable, but the token is only ~20 bits with no throttle/expiry observed -> brute-forceable in principle. Not a takeover primitive on its own; noted as hardening, not a confirmed exploitable finding.",
      "remediation": {
        "summary": "Hardening: add rate-limiting and short expiry to the email-verification code, or widen it."
      }
    }
  ],
